  "title": "Sascha Martin's Ripping News",
  "subtitle": "",
  "description": "Sascha Martin is a young inventor whose genius knows no responsibility. He attends Landfill Public School where, each week during News, he delights and traumatises, horrifies and endangers his classmates in 2M and the entire school community. Sascha's weekly inventions, and the chaos that follows, have won Landfill Public School the widest renown as a Centre of Excellence in Surprise. Now in Sascha Martin's Ripping News , the podcast, each boundary-pushing triumph of science, each inevitable, unanticipated consequence and every edge of your seat apocalypse comes appallingly to life, in the author's own humble narration. Take a few moments in your day. Join Sascha's misadventures with rocket-ships and flying saucers, aliens and dinosaurs, zombies, megafauna and exo-girls, plus his constant, ever critical, always demanding nemesis and not-friend, Mary-Alice Cooper. It's all great fun until somebody ... Well, we'll get to that.",
